{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He answers a word</b> — to those who ask, before they understand, like 'a nation whose tongue you shall not understand' [Deuteronomy 28:49]. The folly will be upon himself. Another interpretation: the folly will be reckoned to him, and the shame — that he shames the one speaking with him or others."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:30.952846830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}